WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:07.872
Captain's Personal Log,
Stardate 517...

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.966
3, uh...

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.567
517...

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.772
4?

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.474
Computer, what day is it?

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.643
Stardate 51721.3.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.449
It's only been two weeks.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.686
I need to talk about this.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:33.825
I have to justify what's
happened, what I've done...

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:36.392
at least to myself.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.337
I can't talk to anyone else...

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.670
not even to Dax.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.869
Maybe if I

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:50.213
just lay it all out in my log,
it'll finally make sense.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.912
I can see
where it all went wrong...

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.852
where I went wrong.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.890
I suppose
it started two weeks ago

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:04.260
while I was posting the weekly
casualty list in the Wardroom.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.731
Every Friday morning
for the past three months

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.233
I've posted the official list

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:12.568
of Starfleet personnel killed,
wounded or missing in the war.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.699
It's become something
of a grim ritual around here.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.835
Not a week goes by

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.175
that someone doesn't find
the name of a loved one

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:24.843
a friend or an acquaintance
on that damned list.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.648
I've grown to hate Fridays.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.557
Who is it, Dax?

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.754
Leslie Wong.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.854
The Skipper of the Cairo?

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.161
She was an instructor
at the Academy

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.531
when I was a sophomore.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.593
Do you know what happened
to the Cairo?

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.400
No, just that she
disappeared on patrol

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.963
in the Romulan Neutral Zone.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:48.996
I'll look into it.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.634
Don't bother... I'm sure

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.837
it's the same old story.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.937
The Jem'Hadar crossed
the Romulan border

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.675
and caught them by surprise.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.377
It's only about the hundredth
time it's happened.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.147
I can't believe
the Romulans allow them

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.983
to violate their territory
so brazenly.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.352
Why do they get away with it?

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.583
The Romulans have a treaty

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.457
of nonaggression and friendship
with the Dominion.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.622
So they're willing to turn
a blind eye to almost anything

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.925
in the name of friendship.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.899
What we need to do is
bring the Romulans

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.195
into the war on our side.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.395
With the combined forces

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.370
of the Federation,
the Klingons and the Romulans

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.894
we could finally
go on the offensive.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.237
That's the last thing
the Romulans want.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.401
Think about it.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.274
They're in
the perfect position.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.676
They get to sit back and watch

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.977
as their biggest rivals
slug it out

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.549
in a long, bloody war.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.608
No one's threatening
their interests.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.483
Why should
they risk their necks?

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.988
There's simply
no reason for them

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.488
to get involved in our war...

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.890
no reason at all.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.292
That was the moment
I made the decision.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.523
It was like I had stepped
through a door

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.895
and locked it behind me.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.901
I was going to bring
the Romulans into the war.

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:49.917
It's in their own best
interests to join the war.

00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:50.978
That's the key.

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:53.853
That's the reason the Romulans
will finally take action

00:04:53.891 --> 00:04:54.983
not to do us any favors

00:04:55.093 --> 00:04:57.687
but to protect themselves
from the Dominion.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:00.994
Okay, let's say
I'm the Romulan Proconsul.

00:05:01.032 --> 00:05:02.124
From where I'm sitting

00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:03.895
the Dominion isn't
a threat to me.

00:05:03.935 --> 00:05:06.130
I have a nonaggression pact
with them.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.603
They are my allies.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:09.106
You're not going
to put your faith

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.573
in some piece of paper, are you?

00:05:10.608 --> 00:05:12.303
Not at all.

00:05:12.343 --> 00:05:13.935
I've been watching them
very closely

00:05:13.978 --> 00:05:15.377
since the beginning of the war

00:05:15.413 --> 00:05:18.746
and so far, they've kept
their part of the bargain.

00:05:18.783 --> 00:05:21.149
They're violating your territory
almost every day.

00:05:21.185 --> 00:05:22.914
What kind of an ally is that?

00:05:22.954 --> 00:05:25.218
So they're crossing my backyard

00:05:25.256 --> 00:05:27.224
to give the Federation
a bloody nose.

00:05:27.258 --> 00:05:29.192
I can't say that makes me feel
very sad.

00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:30.956
You can't be naive enough
to think

00:05:30.995 --> 00:05:33.429
that the Dominion is going
to stop with the Federation.

00:05:33.464 --> 00:05:36.194
When they're finished with us,
they're coming after you.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:38.225
That's speculation.

00:05:38.269 --> 00:05:39.759
The Founders see it
as their sacred duty

00:05:39.804 --> 00:05:41.499
to bring order to the galaxy...
their order.

00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:43.131
Do you think they'll sit idly by

00:05:43.174 --> 00:05:44.869
while you keep
your chaotic empire

00:05:44.909 --> 00:05:47.309
right next
to their perfect order? No.

00:05:47.345 --> 00:05:49.870
If you watch us go under,
then what you're really doing

00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:51.472
is signing
your own death warrant.

00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:54.280
But before I plunge my people
into a conflict

00:05:54.318 --> 00:05:57.845
that will kill millions
of loyal Romulan citizens

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:00.414
I need something more concrete

00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:04.292
than the self-serving argument
of a Starfleet officer.

00:06:04.328 --> 00:06:06.922
I need proof
of Dominion duplicity.

00:06:06.964 --> 00:06:09.455
Not more words...

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.831
proof.

00:06:16.474 --> 00:06:18.203
Very good, old man.

00:06:18.242 --> 00:06:19.971
You would have made
a decent Romulan.

00:06:21.412 --> 00:06:24.609
I prefer the spots
to the pointed ears.

00:06:26.117 --> 00:06:28.415
Okay, you've convinced me.

00:06:28.453 --> 00:06:30.148
They're going to need evidence.

00:06:32.323 --> 00:06:34.348
But if there is evidence

00:06:34.392 --> 00:06:37.384
of a Dominion plan
to attack Romulus

00:06:37.428 --> 00:06:39.919
it's probably buried
deep in the bowels

00:06:39.964 --> 00:06:42.592
of their headquarters
on Cardassia Prime.

00:06:42.633 --> 00:06:45.329
Not exactly the most accessible
place in the galaxy.

00:06:46.804 --> 00:06:48.396
Hmm...

00:06:50.374 --> 00:06:54.242
Not for us, maybe, but there is
someone on this station

00:06:54.278 --> 00:06:56.473
who specializes
in gaining access

00:06:56.514 --> 00:06:58.812
to places
where he is not welcome.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.512
I must say I'm flattered,
Captain.

00:07:01.552 --> 00:07:05.545
I had no idea you held such
a lofty opinion of me.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.615
Your faith in my ability

00:07:07.658 --> 00:07:09.592
to retrieve
classified information

00:07:09.627 --> 00:07:12.152
from my former homeland
is most gratifying.

00:07:12.196 --> 00:07:15.131
Mr. Garak, let's dispense
with the usual repartee

00:07:15.166 --> 00:07:17.396
and concentrate
on the issue at hand.

00:07:17.435 --> 00:07:18.959
Can you do it or not?

00:07:20.738 --> 00:07:24.674
No one wants to see the Dominion
destroyed more than I do

00:07:24.709 --> 00:07:26.870
but to go to Cardassia Prime

00:07:26.911 --> 00:07:29.209
penetrate one of the most
heavily guarded facilities

00:07:29.247 --> 00:07:32.375
in the Quadrant,
steal top secret war plans

00:07:32.416 --> 00:07:34.543
and then return them
safely to you

00:07:34.585 --> 00:07:36.644
is not just another job.

00:07:36.687 --> 00:07:38.712
It's more like a suicide mission

00:07:38.756 --> 00:07:44.092
and that is well outside
my field of expertise.

00:07:45.897 --> 00:07:49.230
I didn't say you had
to go there yourself.

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:52.259
I have to believe
that a man like you

00:07:52.303 --> 00:07:55.136
still has a few contacts
at home...

00:07:55.173 --> 00:07:58.574
a colleague
from the Obsidian Order...

00:07:58.609 --> 00:08:01.169
an old friend...

00:08:01.212 --> 00:08:03.908
a reliable informant...

00:08:03.948 --> 00:08:06.678
someone who might owe you
a favor.

00:08:06.717 --> 00:08:08.617
Perhaps.

00:08:08.653 --> 00:08:12.020
Then I'd say it's time
to call in a favor.

00:08:12.056 --> 00:08:15.787
It would mean calling in
all my favors, Captain.

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:18.352
To do what you're asking
would use up

00:08:18.396 --> 00:08:23.459
every resource I have left
on Cardassia.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:25.628
And it may be...

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:28.935
a very messy,
very bloody business.

00:08:29.006 --> 00:08:31.770
Are you prepared for that?

00:08:34.579 --> 00:08:37.946
I posted my 14th casualty
list this morning.

00:08:38.015 --> 00:08:39.642
I'm already involved

00:08:39.684 --> 00:08:43.586
in a very messy,
very bloody business.

00:08:44.589 --> 00:08:47.114
And the only way
I can see to end it

00:08:47.158 --> 00:08:49.626
is to bring the Romulans
into the war.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.060
I am prepared to do
whatever it takes

00:08:52.096 --> 00:08:55.588
to accomplish that goal,
but I can't do it alone.

00:08:55.633 --> 00:08:57.828
I need help.

00:08:57.869 --> 00:08:59.734
Now...

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.170
are you in or out?

00:09:05.109 --> 00:09:07.236
I'm in.

00:09:07.278 --> 00:09:09.473
My father used to say
that the road to hell

00:09:09.513 --> 00:09:11.947
is paved with good intentions.

00:09:13.317 --> 00:09:16.309
I laid the first stone
right there.

00:09:17.722 --> 00:09:19.485
I'd committed myself.

00:09:19.523 --> 00:09:22.617
I'd pay any price,
go to any lengths

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.924
because my cause was righteous.

00:09:26.364 --> 00:09:30.095
My... intentions were good.

00:09:31.802 --> 00:09:35.067
In the beginning,
that seemed like enough.

00:09:41.178 --> 00:09:43.806
If there's one thing
I've learned over the years

00:09:43.847 --> 00:09:45.940
it's that bad news
invariably comes

00:09:45.983 --> 00:09:47.951
in the middle of the night.

00:09:48.018 --> 00:09:49.815
Kira to Captain Sisko.

00:09:51.989 --> 00:09:53.923
Go ahead, Major.

00:09:53.958 --> 00:09:55.823
We just received a priority one
communication

00:09:55.859 --> 00:09:57.827
from Starfleet Command.

00:09:57.861 --> 00:09:59.829
The Dominion
has invaded Betazed.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.926
According to initial reports,
the invasion force

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.564
must have come from somewhere
in the Calandra Sector.

00:10:08.605 --> 00:10:11.540
Did Starfleet Intelligence
know anything about the buildup?

00:10:11.575 --> 00:10:13.873
No. They believed
Calandra was too far

00:10:13.911 --> 00:10:15.811
from the Dominion supply lines
to be a threat.

00:10:15.846 --> 00:10:17.973
There's plenty of blame
to go around.

00:10:18.015 --> 00:10:20.449
The Tenth Fleet was supposed
to be protecting Betazed

00:10:20.484 --> 00:10:21.712
and its outlying colonies.

00:10:21.752 --> 00:10:24.516
But it was caught out of
position on a training exercise.

00:10:24.555 --> 00:10:27.115
What's worse, Betazed's
own defense systems

00:10:27.157 --> 00:10:28.419
are obsolete and undermanned.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:31.986
The planet was theirs
in less than ten hours.

00:10:32.096 --> 00:10:33.393
With Betazed in the hands

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.830
of the Jem'Hadar,
the Dominion is in a position

00:10:35.866 --> 00:10:39.802
to threaten Vulcan,
Andor, Tellar, Alpha Centauri.

00:10:39.837 --> 00:10:43.568
If we ever needed a new ally,
it's right now.

00:10:50.881 --> 00:10:52.178
Mr. Garak.

00:10:52.216 --> 00:10:53.444
It's been three days.

00:10:53.484 --> 00:10:55.008
Have you made any progress?

00:10:55.119 --> 00:10:57.587
Well, I suppose that depends
on how you look at it.

00:10:57.621 --> 00:10:58.883
This is how I look at it:

00:10:58.922 --> 00:11:01.015
Betazed has just fallen
to the Dominion

00:11:01.058 --> 00:11:02.650
and we need to get
this operation underway.

00:11:02.693 --> 00:11:05.127
I share your desire
for swift action, Captain.

00:11:05.162 --> 00:11:07.392
In fact,
after our last conversation

00:11:07.431 --> 00:11:10.457
I made a few discreet inquiries
among my former associates

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:12.128
still living on Cardassia.

00:11:12.169 --> 00:11:13.466
As I anticipated

00:11:13.504 --> 00:11:16.564
they shared my loathing
for the current government

00:11:16.607 --> 00:11:18.632
and were willing to take on
any assignment

00:11:18.675 --> 00:11:20.540
aimed at its destruction.

00:11:20.577 --> 00:11:22.306
That sounds like progress to me.

00:11:22.346 --> 00:11:23.313
Doesn't it?

00:11:23.347 --> 00:11:26.248
Unfortunately,
they're all dead now.

00:11:26.283 --> 00:11:27.250
What?

00:11:27.284 --> 00:11:28.546
Yes.

00:11:28.585 --> 00:11:31.520
All killed within one day
of speaking with me.

00:11:31.555 --> 00:11:33.614
I suppose that's a testament

00:11:33.657 --> 00:11:36.125
to the effectiveness
of Dominion Security.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.152
One should admire
such efficiency.

00:11:39.196 --> 00:11:40.254
Oh.

00:11:40.297 --> 00:11:42.788
I'm sorry.

00:11:42.833 --> 00:11:44.824
I hope you're not
giving up that easily.

00:11:44.868 --> 00:11:48.304
After all, the stakes
are much higher

00:11:48.338 --> 00:11:49.737
than a few dead operatives.

00:11:49.773 --> 00:11:53.265
The fate of the entire Quadrant
hangs in the balance...

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:56.768
or at least that's the case
you made to me.

00:11:56.814 --> 00:11:58.304
Do you have another plan?

00:11:58.348 --> 00:12:02.114
As a matter of fact, I do

00:12:02.152 --> 00:12:05.212
but I suspect
you won't like it.

00:12:05.255 --> 00:12:06.449
Try me.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.754
If you want to guarantee
that we obtain evidence

00:12:08.792 --> 00:12:11.283
of a Dominion plot to attack
the Romulans

00:12:11.328 --> 00:12:17.130
I suggest that we manufacture
that evidence ourselves.

00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:19.260
Maybe I should have put a stop
to it right there.

00:12:19.303 --> 00:12:20.361
Maybe I should have said

00:12:20.404 --> 00:12:22.668
"Thank you very much
for your input, Mr. Garak.

00:12:22.706 --> 00:12:25.197
I will take your suggestion
under advisement"

00:12:25.242 --> 00:12:27.972
and gone back to my office
and forgotten the whole thing

00:12:28.045 --> 00:12:29.808
but I didn't...

00:12:29.847 --> 00:12:35.183
because in my heart, I knew
what he was saying made sense.

00:12:35.219 --> 00:12:36.982
His name is Vreenak.

00:12:38.989 --> 00:12:39.978
He's been a key member

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.285
of the Romulan Senate
for the past 14 years.

00:12:42.326 --> 00:12:44.726
He's Secretary
of the War Plans Council

00:12:44.761 --> 00:12:46.160
Vice Chairman of the Tal Shiar

00:12:46.196 --> 00:12:49.996
and one of the most trusted
advisors to Proconsul Neral.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.829
He's also the man
that negotiated

00:12:51.869 --> 00:12:54.201
the nonaggression pact
with the Dominion.

00:12:54.238 --> 00:12:55.603
Since you're familiar with him

00:12:55.639 --> 00:12:57.402
I'll skip the rest
of his biography.

00:12:57.441 --> 00:13:00.604
What's important is that he
continues to be one of the most

00:13:00.644 --> 00:13:03.442
ardently pro-Dominion voices
in the Senate.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.381
If we can convince him
that the Dominion is a threat

00:13:06.416 --> 00:13:08.441
the rest of the Senate
will follow.

00:13:08.485 --> 00:13:10.419
All right. How?

00:13:10.454 --> 00:13:11.478
Ten days from now

00:13:11.522 --> 00:13:14.286
Senator Vreenak will be
making a trip to Soukara

00:13:14.324 --> 00:13:16.485
for a diplomatic
meeting with Weyoun.

00:13:16.527 --> 00:13:18.961
I am certain
that he can be persuaded

00:13:18.996 --> 00:13:21.362
to make a secret detour to DS9

00:13:21.398 --> 00:13:25.357
if he were invited
by one Captain Benjamin Sisko.

00:13:25.402 --> 00:13:27.734
How do you know
he'll be visiting Soukara?

00:13:27.771 --> 00:13:30.331
There are some things
I'd rather not discuss.

00:13:30.374 --> 00:13:31.500
May I continue?

00:13:31.542 --> 00:13:32.600
Please.

00:13:32.643 --> 00:13:35.111
When Senator Vreenak arrives,
you will show him

00:13:35.145 --> 00:13:37.773
a holographic recording
of a secret meeting

00:13:37.814 --> 00:13:39.805
held at the highest
level of the Dominion

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.614
in which the planned
invasion of Romulus

00:13:42.653 --> 00:13:43.950
is being discussed.

00:13:43.987 --> 00:13:44.976
You will tell the Senator

00:13:45.055 --> 00:13:47.080
that this information
was obtained

00:13:47.124 --> 00:13:48.819
through various covert means

00:13:48.859 --> 00:13:50.793
at great cost
to the Federation.

00:13:50.827 --> 00:13:53.261
At least ten good
men lost their lives

00:13:53.297 --> 00:13:55.731
bringing it across the line...
that sort of thing.

00:13:55.766 --> 00:13:57.996
He will immediately
suspect it's a forgery

00:13:58.068 --> 00:13:59.160
but you will assure him

00:13:59.203 --> 00:14:01.262
that such a thing
would be impossible.

00:14:01.305 --> 00:14:02.397
"You see, Senator

00:14:02.439 --> 00:14:05.033
"this is an official Cardassian
transcript.

00:14:05.075 --> 00:14:08.442
"It was recorded on a one-time
optolythic data rod

00:14:08.478 --> 00:14:10.343
"used for official
record keeping.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:12.905
"These rods are manufactured
only as needed

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.417
"on Cardassia Prime.

00:14:14.451 --> 00:14:17.147
"Information can only be
transcribed on them once

00:14:17.187 --> 00:14:19.451
and then cannot be altered."

00:14:19.489 --> 00:14:21.081
He'll want to examine it.

00:14:21.124 --> 00:14:22.113
Of course.

00:14:22.159 --> 00:14:24.354
And he will discover,
to his amazement

00:14:24.394 --> 00:14:28.296
that it is completely genuine,
at least, so it will appear.

00:14:28.332 --> 00:14:30.095
But in reality?

00:14:30.133 --> 00:14:32.897
You will have handed him
a genuine optolythic data rod

00:14:32.936 --> 00:14:36.337
but it will contain one
of the most perfect forgeries

00:14:36.373 --> 00:14:37.897
ever fashioned.

00:14:37.941 --> 00:14:40.307
I'm still working
on obtaining the data rod

00:14:40.344 --> 00:14:43.973
but I have found the man who
will create the holo-recording.

00:14:44.014 --> 00:14:46.881
You realize I can't authorize
a thing like this on my own.

00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:48.612
I have to clear it
with Starfleet Command.

00:14:48.652 --> 00:14:51.883
Of course, but I suspect
that with the fall of Betazed

00:14:51.922 --> 00:14:53.981
they'll be ready to do
whatever it takes

00:14:54.024 --> 00:14:56.322
to bring the Romulans
into the war.

00:15:00.063 --> 00:15:01.690
I'll let you know.

00:15:01.732 --> 00:15:03.427
Uh, one last thing, Captain.

00:15:03.467 --> 00:15:07.403
The man we need to forge
this holo-program

00:15:07.437 --> 00:15:09.337
is currently sitting
in a Klingon prison

00:15:09.373 --> 00:15:10.465
awaiting execution.

00:15:10.507 --> 00:15:13.237
To save time
and, incidentally, his life

00:15:13.277 --> 00:15:15.609
I thought that perhaps
you could contact

00:15:15.646 --> 00:15:19.138
Chancellor Gowron today
and arrange a pardon?

00:15:19.182 --> 00:15:20.649
What's his name?

00:15:20.684 --> 00:15:22.948
Grathon Tolar.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:27.514
I cannot tell you
how grateful I am, Captain.

00:15:27.557 --> 00:15:30.958
The Klingons were going
to execute me tomorrow.

00:15:31.028 --> 00:15:33.155
Of course, they say
that every day.

00:15:33.196 --> 00:15:35.289
It's one of the little
games they like to play.

00:15:36.433 --> 00:15:38.958
You do understand the terms
of your parole.

00:15:39.036 --> 00:15:40.367
Oh, yes.

00:15:40.404 --> 00:15:43.635
I have to promise to stay
away from the Klingon Empire.

00:15:44.675 --> 00:15:45.835
That'll be tough.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.207
And I have to create

00:15:48.245 --> 00:15:53.080
some kind of a special
holo-program for you.

00:15:54.184 --> 00:15:55.481
Well, I can hardly wait.

00:15:55.519 --> 00:15:57.885
I've never worked
for Starfleet before.

00:15:57.921 --> 00:15:59.786
Let's be very clear about this.

00:15:59.823 --> 00:16:01.882
You're not working
for Starfleet.

00:16:01.925 --> 00:16:04.325
This entire matter
is off the record.

00:16:04.361 --> 00:16:07.421
As far as you're concerned,
you're working for me.

00:16:07.464 --> 00:16:09.193
Oh, a personal matter.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.765
Something special,
for your eyes only?

00:16:13.804 --> 00:16:15.795
Something with, perhaps

00:16:15.839 --> 00:16:19.866
five or six Orion slave girls
and... oh...

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.899
Mr. Tolar.

00:16:20.944 --> 00:16:24.539
I suggest you go
and wait in your quarters.

00:16:24.581 --> 00:16:26.071
Mr. Garak will provide you
with all

00:16:26.116 --> 00:16:27.674
the information you need.

00:16:27.718 --> 00:16:30.209
Garak... is here?

00:16:30.253 --> 00:16:31.914
That's right.

00:16:31.955 --> 00:16:34.753
Oh... oh...

00:16:34.791 --> 00:16:38.750
Well... that's different.

00:16:41.598 --> 00:16:43.930
I'll wait in my quarters.

00:16:45.936 --> 00:16:47.096
Why I didn't listen

00:16:47.137 --> 00:16:48.798
to the voice
in the back of my mind

00:16:48.839 --> 00:16:50.966
telling me not to believe
a word he said

00:16:51.041 --> 00:16:52.303
I'll never know.

00:16:52.342 --> 00:16:54.970
But it didn't take long
for me to come face-to-face

00:16:55.045 --> 00:16:57.912
with the fact
that I'd made a mistake.

00:16:57.948 --> 00:16:59.848
Odo to the Captain.

00:16:59.883 --> 00:17:01.214
Go ahead, Constable.

00:17:01.251 --> 00:17:02.513
I'm sorry to disturb you

00:17:02.552 --> 00:17:05.077
but do you know a man
named Grathon Tolar?

00:17:05.122 --> 00:17:06.817
Yes. Why do you ask?

00:17:06.857 --> 00:17:09.348
Because he just tried
to kill Quark.

00:17:17.233 --> 00:17:19.827
Sit still, Quark.
You'll be fine.

00:17:21.504 --> 00:17:23.335
All right, keep an eye on him.

00:17:24.941 --> 00:17:26.340
What happened?

00:17:26.375 --> 00:17:29.833
As I understand it, Mr. Tolar
over there came in

00:17:29.879 --> 00:17:30.937
about two hours ago

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.242
ordered a bottle
of Whelan bitters.

00:17:32.281 --> 00:17:35.717
15 minutes later,
he ordered a second bottle

00:17:35.751 --> 00:17:37.275
and then a third.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.947
Halfway through
his fourth bottle

00:17:39.021 --> 00:17:42.218
he decided to dance
with M'Pella.

00:17:42.258 --> 00:17:44.590
She was otherwise
engaged, running

00:17:44.627 --> 00:17:46.595
the dabo wheel,
declined his invitation.

00:17:46.629 --> 00:17:48.494
He decided to force the issue.

00:17:48.531 --> 00:17:52.968
A brief struggle ensued,
and Quark

00:17:53.035 --> 00:17:55.595
in an uncharacteristic
display of chivalry

00:17:55.638 --> 00:17:59.335
attempted to intervene,
so Tolar stabbed him.

00:17:59.375 --> 00:18:00.933
Normally, he'd be

00:18:00.977 --> 00:18:03.070
sitting in a holding
cell, but he claims

00:18:03.112 --> 00:18:04.773
he's a friend of yours.

00:18:04.814 --> 00:18:06.338
He's no friend of mine...

00:18:06.382 --> 00:18:08.213
but he is working for me.

00:18:08.251 --> 00:18:10.412
It's an extremely
sensitive matter

00:18:10.453 --> 00:18:12.444
concerning Federation security.

00:18:12.488 --> 00:18:15.855
I can't have any record
of him being on the station.

00:18:16.893 --> 00:18:17.951
I see.

00:18:19.328 --> 00:18:21.888
I am certainly aware
of the need

00:18:21.931 --> 00:18:24.798
for special security measures
during wartime

00:18:24.834 --> 00:18:26.665
but, as a matter of law

00:18:26.702 --> 00:18:30.433
if Quark chooses
to press charges against Tolar

00:18:30.473 --> 00:18:33.203
I have no choice
but to make an arrest.

00:18:33.242 --> 00:18:34.732
May I speak to Quark?

00:18:38.981 --> 00:18:39.948
How is he?

00:18:39.982 --> 00:18:40.949
How do I look?

00:18:41.017 --> 00:18:42.951
I'm a man who just
had a brush with death.

00:18:43.019 --> 00:18:44.111
He'll be fine.

00:18:44.153 --> 00:18:46.280
His ribs deflected the knife
from his major organs.

00:18:46.322 --> 00:18:47.812
Bleeding was superficial.

00:18:47.857 --> 00:18:48.949
Superficial?

00:18:48.991 --> 00:18:51.425
Do you know how much
this shirt cost?

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.690
Will you excuse us
for a moment, Doctor?

00:18:53.729 --> 00:18:54.991
I'll check on you tomorrow.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.497
Do you intend to press charges?

00:19:03.539 --> 00:19:05.268
You bet I do.

00:19:05.308 --> 00:19:08.141
What will it take, um...

00:19:10.012 --> 00:19:12.742
to, uh, convince you otherwise?

00:19:12.782 --> 00:19:14.875
Are you offering me...

00:19:14.917 --> 00:19:16.077
a bribe?

00:19:19.822 --> 00:19:21.653
I knew it.

00:19:21.691 --> 00:19:24.558
Captain, I've always liked you.

00:19:24.594 --> 00:19:27.085
I suspected that somewhere deep
down in your heart of hearts

00:19:27.129 --> 00:19:29.188
there was a tiny bit of Ferengi
just waiting to get out.

00:19:29.231 --> 00:19:30.459
What's your price?

00:19:30.499 --> 00:19:34.333
Well... let's start
with replacing my clothes

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.496
and M'Pella's clothes.

00:19:35.538 --> 00:19:36.869
All right.

00:19:36.906 --> 00:19:38.840
I'm not finished.

00:19:38.874 --> 00:19:41.468
I think I should be compensated

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.535
for the loss of business
I suffered today

00:19:43.579 --> 00:19:47.572
which I calculate
as no less than...

00:19:47.617 --> 00:19:51.018
five bars
of gold-pressed latinum.

00:19:52.755 --> 00:19:53.949
Done.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:57.949
I'm also having a problem
with Station Security.

00:19:58.027 --> 00:20:01.394
They're holding
some cargo containers

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:02.624
which I've been waiting for

00:20:02.665 --> 00:20:06.795
because of some missing
import license or something.

00:20:06.836 --> 00:20:08.064
I'll handle it.

00:20:08.104 --> 00:20:09.901
A-anything else?

00:20:09.939 --> 00:20:10.906
No.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:15.070
I think we can call it a bribe.

00:20:15.111 --> 00:20:16.976
And thank you, Captain.

00:20:17.046 --> 00:20:21.415
Thank you for restoring my faith
in the 98th Rule of Acquisition.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.647
"Every man has his price."

00:20:30.259 --> 00:20:33.387
That was my first moment
of real doubt...

00:20:33.429 --> 00:20:35.989
when I started to wonder...

00:20:36.098 --> 00:20:39.397
if this whole thing
was a mistake.

00:20:42.138 --> 00:20:45.107
So then I went back
to my office...

00:20:46.709 --> 00:20:49.007
and there...

00:20:49.045 --> 00:20:53.141
was a new casualty list
waiting for me.

00:20:56.385 --> 00:21:00.754
People are dying
out there every day!

00:21:02.058 --> 00:21:04.754
Entire worlds are struggling
for their freedom

00:21:04.794 --> 00:21:07.422
and here I am, still worrying

00:21:07.463 --> 00:21:10.432
about the finer points
of morality.

00:21:10.466 --> 00:21:15.062
No, I... I had to keep my eye
on the ball.

00:21:15.104 --> 00:21:17.299
Winning the war,
stopping the bloodshed...

00:21:17.339 --> 00:21:19.466
those were the priorities!

00:21:19.508 --> 00:21:21.237
So I pushed on

00:21:21.277 --> 00:21:23.245
and every time another doubt
appeared before me

00:21:23.279 --> 00:21:26.146
I just found another way
to shove it aside.

00:21:26.182 --> 00:21:28.275
Mind if I join you?

00:21:29.452 --> 00:21:30.612
Be my guest.

00:21:34.623 --> 00:21:35.817
Ops.

00:21:35.858 --> 00:21:37.257
Hold. The less I'm seen

00:21:37.293 --> 00:21:39.284
parading through Ops,
the better.

00:21:39.328 --> 00:21:40.989
I couldn't agree more.

00:21:41.097 --> 00:21:42.655
You seem angry.

00:21:42.698 --> 00:21:44.290
Who's watching Tolar?

00:21:44.333 --> 00:21:45.766
I've locked him in his quarters.

00:21:45.801 --> 00:21:47.894
I've also left him
with the distinct impression

00:21:47.937 --> 00:21:49.837
that if he attempts
to force the door open

00:21:49.872 --> 00:21:51.965
it may explode.

00:21:52.007 --> 00:21:53.338
I hope that's
just an impression.

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:56.811
It's best not to dwell
on such minutiae.

00:21:56.846 --> 00:22:00.612
In any case, we have far more
important matters to discuss.

00:22:00.649 --> 00:22:02.810
I've located a gentleman
willing to sell us

00:22:02.852 --> 00:22:05.514
a genuine optolythic data rod.

00:22:05.554 --> 00:22:06.953
How do you know it's genuine?

00:22:07.022 --> 00:22:09.115
I trust the source,
but rest assured

00:22:09.158 --> 00:22:11.649
I will confirm
the rod's authenticity

00:22:11.694 --> 00:22:15.494
before I make payment,
which brings me to you.

00:22:15.531 --> 00:22:16.964
How much does he want?

00:22:17.032 --> 00:22:20.593
I'm afraid he's not
interested in latinum.

00:22:20.636 --> 00:22:22.263
The gentleman in question

00:22:22.304 --> 00:22:24.772
has requested
to be compensated with...

00:22:25.775 --> 00:22:28.801
200 liters of biomimetic gel.

00:22:28.844 --> 00:22:29.970
What?!

00:22:30.045 --> 00:22:32.240
I don't know why, exactly.

00:22:32.281 --> 00:22:34.272
One would assume
it has something to do

00:22:34.316 --> 00:22:35.874
with genetic experimentation.

00:22:35.918 --> 00:22:37.510
Offer him something else.

00:22:37.553 --> 00:22:39.748
Believe me, I wouldn't
be relaying this request

00:22:39.789 --> 00:22:42.314
if I thought
he'd take something else.

00:22:42.358 --> 00:22:45.384
Biomimetic gel is strictly
controlled by the Federation

00:22:45.427 --> 00:22:47.418
and not for sale at any price.

00:22:47.463 --> 00:22:50.330
Find someone else
who's willing to sell us a rod.

00:22:50.366 --> 00:22:51.526
I wasn't exaggerating

00:22:51.567 --> 00:22:53.831
when I told you
about the near impossibility

00:22:53.869 --> 00:22:57.361
of obtaining a genuine
Cardassian data rod.

00:22:57.406 --> 00:22:58.998
It's something
of a minor miracle

00:22:59.074 --> 00:23:01.406
that I was able
to locate this one source.

00:23:01.443 --> 00:23:04.901
I'm virtually certain
I won't find another.

00:23:04.947 --> 00:23:08.508
I'm afraid we either
give him what he wants

00:23:08.551 --> 00:23:12.419
or forget the whole enterprise.

00:23:14.056 --> 00:23:15.580
Then let's forget about it.

00:23:15.624 --> 00:23:16.613
Ops.

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:19.691
Hold.

00:23:19.728 --> 00:23:21.958
200 liters is
out of the question.

00:23:22.031 --> 00:23:25.933
There's not that much gel
in the entire sector.

00:23:25.968 --> 00:23:30.496
I believe that the quantity
is open to negotiation.

00:23:35.678 --> 00:23:37.873
Ops.

00:23:37.913 --> 00:23:39.107
Captain, biomimetic gel

00:23:39.148 --> 00:23:41.173
is an extremely dangerous
compound, as you know.

00:23:41.217 --> 00:23:43.082
I can't release it
without at least some idea

00:23:43.118 --> 00:23:44.085
of where it's going.

00:23:44.119 --> 00:23:45.609
In the wrong hands,
it could be used

00:23:45.654 --> 00:23:48.282
to make biogenic weapons,
or for illegal

00:23:48.324 --> 00:23:50.292
replication experiments or to
develop organic explosives...

00:23:50.326 --> 00:23:52.260
Perhaps I didn't
make myself clear, Doctor.

00:23:52.294 --> 00:23:54.421
This is not a request;
it's an order.

00:23:54.463 --> 00:23:56.897
You will package
85 liters of biomimetic gel

00:23:56.932 --> 00:24:00.424
for interstellar transport,
and deliver them to Cargo Bay 3.

00:24:00.469 --> 00:24:01.731
Is that understood?

00:24:02.671 --> 00:24:04.298
Yes.

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:06.865
I'd like this order
in writing, please, sir.

00:24:10.646 --> 00:24:12.307
I thought you might.

00:24:14.917 --> 00:24:16.942
You should know
that I shall note this in my log

00:24:17.019 --> 00:24:19.920
and file an official protest
with Starfleet Medical.

00:24:19.955 --> 00:24:21.946
That is your right,
but I want the gel

00:24:21.991 --> 00:24:23.185
by the end of the day.

00:24:23.225 --> 00:24:24.214
Dismissed.

00:24:30.933 --> 00:24:32.093
The Founders have decided

00:24:32.134 --> 00:24:34.864
to implement stage two
ahead of schedule.

00:24:34.904 --> 00:24:36.701
The invasion of Romulus?

00:24:36.739 --> 00:24:38.764
It's too soon.

00:24:38.808 --> 00:24:40.571
We're engaged in heavy fighting

00:24:40.609 --> 00:24:42.600
all along the border
with the Federation.

00:24:42.645 --> 00:24:44.670
The Klingons are preparing
to go on the offensive, and...

00:24:44.713 --> 00:24:45.737
Fortunately, the Founders

00:24:45.781 --> 00:24:47.476
have better vision than you do.

00:24:47.516 --> 00:24:49.882
They can see the opportunities
before us

00:24:49.919 --> 00:24:51.181
even when you cannot.

00:24:51.220 --> 00:24:53.620
Consider...

00:24:53.656 --> 00:24:57.990
the Romulans don't expect
an attack from Cardassia.

00:24:58.093 --> 00:25:01.153
The bulk of the Romulan fleet
is still deployed

00:25:01.197 --> 00:25:03.529
along the Neutral Zone
with the Federation.

00:25:03.566 --> 00:25:06.160
The Founders estimate
we could be on Romulus itself

00:25:06.202 --> 00:25:07.931
in less than three weeks.

00:25:07.970 --> 00:25:09.437
Three weeks?

00:25:09.471 --> 00:25:11.439
I heard
the same kind of estimates

00:25:11.473 --> 00:25:13.441
before we attacked
the Federation.

00:25:13.475 --> 00:25:14.703
Those plans were ruined

00:25:14.743 --> 00:25:17.268
by the incompetency
of your predecessor.

00:25:17.313 --> 00:25:19.304
Gul Dukat is a great man.

00:25:19.348 --> 00:25:22.340
Gul Dukat is a preening egotist
and a fool.

00:25:22.384 --> 00:25:23.851
We offered him
unchallenged control

00:25:23.886 --> 00:25:25.444
of the Alpha Quadrant, and all

00:25:25.487 --> 00:25:27.546
he could think about
was his daughter.

00:25:32.661 --> 00:25:35.721
Now, shall we get back
to the business at hand?

00:25:35.764 --> 00:25:36.731
That's it.

00:25:36.765 --> 00:25:38.130
Freeze program.

00:25:40.369 --> 00:25:41.836
That's all the new material.

00:25:41.871 --> 00:25:44.897
The rest of the program plays
exactly as you saw before.

00:25:44.940 --> 00:25:46.168
What do you think?

00:25:46.208 --> 00:25:48.335
It's, uh, better.

00:25:48.377 --> 00:25:49.708
They seem more real.

00:25:49.745 --> 00:25:51.736
Yes, and all I had to do
was add

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:54.544
a little petty bickering
and mutual loathing.

00:25:54.583 --> 00:25:57.074
So, you are happy.

00:25:58.287 --> 00:26:00.983
It's... satisfactory.

00:26:01.023 --> 00:26:04.356
You may record the program
onto the data rod now.

00:26:09.265 --> 00:26:11.426
I received a message.

00:26:11.467 --> 00:26:13.526
Senator Vreenak is on the way.

00:26:13.569 --> 00:26:14.558
Excellent.

00:26:18.707 --> 00:26:19.674
Done.

00:26:21.577 --> 00:26:23.204
Who gets it?

00:26:23.245 --> 00:26:27.682
Just... put it in the case.

00:26:27.716 --> 00:26:28.683
Ah.

00:26:34.690 --> 00:26:38.126
Well... it has been a pleasure

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:40.560
doing business
with you gentlemen.

00:26:40.596 --> 00:26:42.086
Call me again if you ever...

00:26:42.131 --> 00:26:43.723
You're not going anywhere.

00:26:43.766 --> 00:26:46.200
What...?
What do you mean?

00:26:46.235 --> 00:26:47.634
I mean, you're not leaving

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:50.537
until your work is accepted
by our client.

00:26:50.572 --> 00:26:52.130
Well, that isn't fair.

00:26:52.174 --> 00:26:54.267
You can't keep me here
against my will.

00:26:54.310 --> 00:26:55.971
I haven't done anything wrong.

00:26:56.045 --> 00:26:58.479
We had an agreement!

00:26:58.514 --> 00:26:59.981
I'm making a new agreement.

00:27:00.082 --> 00:27:03.142
If that program passes
inspection, you walk free

00:27:03.185 --> 00:27:06.018
but if there is even
the slightest flaw

00:27:06.055 --> 00:27:08.785
then I will send you back
to that Klingon prison

00:27:08.824 --> 00:27:12.419
and tell Gowron to take his
time while he executes you.

00:27:12.461 --> 00:27:14.929
All right. It will pass.

00:27:14.997 --> 00:27:16.055
You'll see.

00:27:17.333 --> 00:27:20.598
It... will... pass.

00:27:20.636 --> 00:27:22.604
I sincerely hope so.

00:27:22.638 --> 00:27:25.368
Now, why don't you go back
to your quarters?

00:27:25.407 --> 00:27:29.241
I'll be along shortly
to say... hello.

00:27:39.855 --> 00:27:43.416
Maybe I was under more pressure
than I realized.

00:27:43.459 --> 00:27:46.019
Maybe it was really starting
to get to me.

00:27:47.629 --> 00:27:50.723
But I was off the hook.

00:27:50.766 --> 00:27:54.964
Starfleet Command had given
the plan their blessing

00:27:55.070 --> 00:27:57.868
and I thought
that would make things easier.

00:28:01.810 --> 00:28:06.247
But I was the one
who had to make it happen.

00:28:06.281 --> 00:28:12.845
I was the one who had to look
Senator Vreenak in his eye...

00:28:12.888 --> 00:28:16.324
and convince him that a lie...

00:28:16.358 --> 00:28:18.519
was the truth.

00:28:18.560 --> 00:28:21.893
So while you're entertaining
the Senator in the Wardroom

00:28:21.930 --> 00:28:22.897
I'll take the opportunity

00:28:22.931 --> 00:28:24.489
to make a quick search
of his ship's database.

00:28:24.533 --> 00:28:25.557
For what?

00:28:25.601 --> 00:28:27.125
Well, for any intelligence
information

00:28:27.169 --> 00:28:29.729
he may have picked up
on the Dominion in Soukara.

00:28:29.772 --> 00:28:31.069
What if you get caught?

00:28:31.106 --> 00:28:32.300
Oh, I think
that's highly unlikely.

00:28:32.341 --> 00:28:34.309
I doubt the Senator
will be traveling

00:28:34.343 --> 00:28:36.675
with more than four bodyguards
at the most.

00:28:36.712 --> 00:28:38.942
Two will stand watch
outside the Wardroom

00:28:38.981 --> 00:28:40.949
and two will stay
in the landing bay.

00:28:41.050 --> 00:28:44.417
I assure you, they'll never know
I was even near their ship.

00:28:44.453 --> 00:28:47.047
Just make sure
you don't get caught.

00:28:54.329 --> 00:28:55.557
Report.

00:28:55.597 --> 00:28:57.258
Sections 52 Baker
through 62 Baker

00:28:57.299 --> 00:28:58.323
have been secured.

00:28:58.367 --> 00:29:00.927
I have posted armed guards
at every entry point

00:29:00.969 --> 00:29:03.199
and I have personally scanned
all compartments

00:29:03.238 --> 00:29:04.705
for signs
of surveillance equipment.

00:29:04.740 --> 00:29:06.105
Very good, Commander.

00:29:06.141 --> 00:29:09.838
Maintain current security
measures until further notice.

00:29:09.878 --> 00:29:12.904
No one is to enter this area
except Mr. Garak and myself.

00:29:12.948 --> 00:29:13.915
Aye, sir.

00:29:13.949 --> 00:29:15.712
Always a pleasure
to see you, Mr. Worf.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:20.915
Ops to Captain Sisko.

00:29:21.023 --> 00:29:22.047
Go ahead, Major.

00:29:22.091 --> 00:29:24.116
We've just received
the coded subspace signal

00:29:24.159 --> 00:29:25.319
you were waiting for.

00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:26.327
Should I reply?

00:29:26.361 --> 00:29:27.919
No reply, Major.

00:29:27.963 --> 00:29:28.987
Sisko out.

00:30:10.772 --> 00:30:13.240
I'll take my leave of you now,
Captain.

00:30:13.275 --> 00:30:15.266
Oh, and one last thing.

00:30:15.310 --> 00:30:17.778
Vreenak believes
he's on the winning side

00:30:17.813 --> 00:30:19.974
so until you can prove otherwise

00:30:20.048 --> 00:30:23.142
you may have to put up
with a certain...

00:30:23.185 --> 00:30:24.152
acerbic attitude.

00:30:24.186 --> 00:30:25.551
Uh, Mr. Garak

00:30:25.587 --> 00:30:27.851
after having spent
a week with you

00:30:27.890 --> 00:30:31.485
I have developed
a very, very thick skin.

00:30:31.527 --> 00:30:33.495
Good luck.

00:30:45.908 --> 00:30:47.569
Welcome aboard, Senator.

00:30:47.609 --> 00:30:50.339
I'm Captain Benjamin Sisko.

00:30:50.379 --> 00:30:55.146
So, you're the Commander
of Deep Space 9...

00:30:55.184 --> 00:30:57.277
and the Emissary
to the Prophets

00:30:57.319 --> 00:31:01.779
decorated combat officer,
widower, father, mentor.

00:31:01.823 --> 00:31:03.450
And, oh, yes...

00:31:03.492 --> 00:31:05.983
the man who started the war
with the Dominion.

00:31:07.496 --> 00:31:09.623
Somehow I thought
you'd be taller.

00:31:09.665 --> 00:31:11.132
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:31:11.166 --> 00:31:12.326
To be honest

00:31:12.367 --> 00:31:15.461
my opinion of Starfleet officers
is so low

00:31:15.504 --> 00:31:18.302
you'd have to work very hard
indeed to disappoint me.

00:31:18.340 --> 00:31:21.207
If you'll come with me,
I'll show you to your quarters.

00:31:21.243 --> 00:31:23.234
I look forward
to seeing your station...

00:31:23.278 --> 00:31:24.973
while it's still here, that is.

00:31:25.047 --> 00:31:27.709
The way the war's going
with the Federation

00:31:27.749 --> 00:31:29.614
it may not be around
much longer.

00:31:40.261 --> 00:31:41.990
Mmm.

00:31:42.030 --> 00:31:44.396
A fair approximation, but...

00:31:44.432 --> 00:31:47.128
somewhat lacking in aroma.

00:31:47.168 --> 00:31:51.434
Real kali-fal should forcibly
open one's sinuses

00:31:51.472 --> 00:31:53.463
well before the first sip.

00:31:53.508 --> 00:31:55.305
We don't have much experience

00:31:55.343 --> 00:31:57.743
in replicating
Romulan beverages.

00:31:57.779 --> 00:31:59.940
Of course, all of that
would change

00:31:59.981 --> 00:32:03.212
if we became allies
instead of cold warriors.

00:32:04.252 --> 00:32:05.947
You are persistent, Captain.

00:32:06.054 --> 00:32:07.351
I'll grant you that.

00:32:07.388 --> 00:32:09.948
But dogged determination
isn't enough

00:32:10.024 --> 00:32:12.652
to change the reality
of your situation.

00:32:12.693 --> 00:32:17.630
Time is definitely
not on your side.

00:32:17.665 --> 00:32:19.462
The Dominion shipyards
are operating

00:32:19.500 --> 00:32:21.058
at 100 percent capacity.

00:32:21.102 --> 00:32:23.627
Yours are still being rebuilt.

00:32:23.671 --> 00:32:29.735
The Dominion is breeding legions
of Jem'Hadar soldiers every day.

00:32:29.777 --> 00:32:33.235
You're experiencing
a manpower shortage.

00:32:33.281 --> 00:32:35.806
But most important...

00:32:38.419 --> 00:32:44.085
the Dominion is resolved
to win the war at any cost.

00:32:45.526 --> 00:32:46.618
You and I both know

00:32:46.661 --> 00:32:49.596
the Federation has already
put out peace feelers.

00:32:49.630 --> 00:32:51.894
Now, in all candor

00:32:51.933 --> 00:32:55.266
if you were in my position,
which side would you choose?

00:32:55.303 --> 00:32:58.101
I'd pick the side
most likely to leave us in peace

00:32:58.139 --> 00:32:59.834
when the dust settles.

00:32:59.874 --> 00:33:02.536
Maybe you're right.

00:33:02.577 --> 00:33:05.478
Maybe the Dominion will win
in the end.

00:33:05.513 --> 00:33:08.539
Then the Founders will control
what we now call Cardassia

00:33:08.583 --> 00:33:11.575
the Klingon Empire
and the Federation.

00:33:11.619 --> 00:33:14.747
So, instead of facing
three separate opponents

00:33:14.789 --> 00:33:18.520
with three separate agendas,
you'll find yourselves facing

00:33:18.559 --> 00:33:21.289
the same opponent on every side.

00:33:21.329 --> 00:33:23.126
There's a word for that...

00:33:23.164 --> 00:33:24.756
surrounded.

00:33:25.833 --> 00:33:28.961
It really is a good replica.

00:33:29.003 --> 00:33:31.198
The aroma's
starting to grow on me.

00:33:31.239 --> 00:33:33.469
For a moment there, I almost
forgot it wasn't the real thing

00:33:33.508 --> 00:33:35.601
but only for a moment.

00:33:35.643 --> 00:33:38.908
You make
some very good points, Captain

00:33:38.946 --> 00:33:42.541
but it's still
all speculation and theory...

00:33:42.583 --> 00:33:45.984
nothing that would warrant
abrogating our treaty

00:33:46.020 --> 00:33:48.147
and plunging the Empire
into war.

00:33:51.025 --> 00:33:52.993
What if I told you

00:33:53.027 --> 00:33:55.894
that the Dominion
is planning a sneak attack

00:33:55.930 --> 00:33:58.956
on the Romulan Empire
at this very moment?

00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:01.969
Mmm...

00:34:02.003 --> 00:34:04.233
I'd want proof.

00:34:07.708 --> 00:34:09.539
And with the Cardassian
Fourth Order

00:34:09.577 --> 00:34:10.839
protecting their flank

00:34:10.878 --> 00:34:13.472
the 23rd Jem'Hadar division
will begin its thrust

00:34:13.514 --> 00:34:15.277
across the Glintara Sector.

00:34:15.316 --> 00:34:17.477
They should begin
the invasion of Romulus

00:34:17.518 --> 00:34:18.951
on the following day.

00:34:19.053 --> 00:34:21.283
Once we've taken the homeworld

00:34:21.322 --> 00:34:22.949
organized resistance
will crumble

00:34:23.057 --> 00:34:24.957
when outlying
systems and colonies

00:34:24.992 --> 00:34:27.153
begin looking out
for themselves.

00:34:27.195 --> 00:34:28.753
Consolidation
of the entire empire

00:34:28.796 --> 00:34:30.195
will take three months at most.

00:34:30.231 --> 00:34:31.528
What if the Romulan fleet

00:34:31.566 --> 00:34:33.193
reacts faster
than you're anticipating?

00:34:33.234 --> 00:34:34.599
What if they pull
all of their forces

00:34:34.635 --> 00:34:37.798
away from the Federation border
at the first sign of our attack?

00:34:37.838 --> 00:34:39.965
I place my faith
in the Founders.

00:34:40.007 --> 00:34:42.874
They say the Romulans
are not ready for war

00:34:42.910 --> 00:34:45.674
and will not react fast enough
once it begins.

00:34:45.713 --> 00:34:48.978
Now, do you wish
to dispute their judgment?

00:34:50.885 --> 00:34:52.546
No, of course not.

00:34:53.955 --> 00:34:56.981
I serve the Founders.

00:34:57.024 --> 00:34:58.855
As do we all.

00:34:58.893 --> 00:35:00.656
Meeting adjourned.

00:35:07.235 --> 00:35:09.362
I'd like to examine...

00:35:09.403 --> 00:35:11.769
that data rod.

00:35:28.956 --> 00:35:32.483
So all I could do was wait...

00:35:32.526 --> 00:35:38.260
and see how masterful
Tolar's forgery really was.

00:35:42.003 --> 00:35:44.369
So I waited.

00:35:44.405 --> 00:35:47.636
Tried to catch up
on my paperwork.

00:35:51.178 --> 00:35:54.670
But I-I found it very difficult
to focus on...

00:35:54.715 --> 00:35:57.240
criminal activity reports, ha?

00:35:59.654 --> 00:36:02.817
Cargo manifests.

00:36:02.857 --> 00:36:05.087
So I went back to pacing...

00:36:05.126 --> 00:36:07.390
and staring out of the window.

00:36:12.233 --> 00:36:14.599
I'm not an impatient man.

00:36:16.170 --> 00:36:20.368
I'm not one to agonize over
decisions once they're made.

00:36:20.408 --> 00:36:23.036
I got that from my father.

00:36:23.077 --> 00:36:25.602
He always says...

00:36:25.646 --> 00:36:27.307
"Worry and doubt

00:36:27.348 --> 00:36:31.944
"are the greatest enemies
of a great chef.

00:36:31.986 --> 00:36:37.083
"The soufflé will either rise
or it won't.

00:36:37.124 --> 00:36:40.059
"There's not a damn thing
you can do about it

00:36:40.094 --> 00:36:42.961
"so you might as well
just sit back and wait

00:36:43.030 --> 00:36:44.998
and see what happens."

00:36:54.275 --> 00:36:55.936
But this time...

00:36:58.112 --> 00:37:00.808
the cost of failure
was so high...

00:37:03.017 --> 00:37:05.918
I found it difficult
to take his advice.

00:37:05.986 --> 00:37:09.888
If Vreenak discovered that
the data rod was a forgery

00:37:09.924 --> 00:37:11.255
if he realized
that we were trying

00:37:11.292 --> 00:37:13.920
to trick them into the war,
it could push the Romulans

00:37:13.994 --> 00:37:16.258
even farther
into the enemy camp.

00:37:16.297 --> 00:37:18.925
They could start
to openly help the Dominion.

00:37:18.966 --> 00:37:20.524
If worse came to worst

00:37:20.568 --> 00:37:23.059
they could actually join
the war against us.

00:37:23.104 --> 00:37:24.571
I had the distinct feeling

00:37:24.605 --> 00:37:26.470
that victory or defeat
would be decided

00:37:26.507 --> 00:37:27.701
in the next few minutes.

00:37:38.652 --> 00:37:40.711
It's a fake!

00:37:49.729 --> 00:37:53.028
So, it all blew up in my face.

00:37:54.967 --> 00:37:59.961
And all the lies
and compromises...

00:38:00.006 --> 00:38:02.236
the inner doubts
and rationalizations...

00:38:02.275 --> 00:38:04.539
all for nothing.

00:38:04.577 --> 00:38:08.172
Vreenak was furious.

00:38:08.214 --> 00:38:10.375
I can't say I blamed him.

00:38:10.416 --> 00:38:12.509
I'd have reacted the same way.

00:38:15.188 --> 00:38:17.679
After telling me
in no uncertain terms

00:38:17.724 --> 00:38:20.420
that he would expose
this "vile deception"

00:38:20.460 --> 00:38:22.428
to the entire Alpha Quadrant

00:38:22.462 --> 00:38:25.431
he got back in his shuttle
and headed home.

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:30.501
There didn't seem
to be anything more to do.

00:38:30.536 --> 00:38:32.731
So, I went back to work.

00:38:32.772 --> 00:38:35.605
Two days later, I got the news.

00:38:39.412 --> 00:38:40.743
No one for me today.

00:38:40.780 --> 00:38:41.838
I had one.

00:38:41.881 --> 00:38:43.644
Maria Tatalia,
wounded in action.

00:38:43.683 --> 00:38:45.344
Friend?

00:38:45.385 --> 00:38:46.784
Friend of a friend.

00:38:46.819 --> 00:38:48.047
Actually, I only met her once.

00:38:48.087 --> 00:38:49.782
I don't think she'd remember me.

00:38:49.822 --> 00:38:51.790
Friend of a friend
between the two of us.

00:38:51.824 --> 00:38:53.553
Well, I know
it sounds a bit strange

00:38:53.593 --> 00:38:56.084
but I'd say we're off
to a pretty good start today.

00:38:56.129 --> 00:38:57.562
Captain, we just received word

00:38:57.597 --> 00:39:00.293
from Starfleet Intelligence
that a Romulan shuttlecraft

00:39:00.333 --> 00:39:03.200
carrying a high-ranking Senator
has just been destroyed.

00:39:03.236 --> 00:39:04.203
Which Senator?

00:39:04.237 --> 00:39:05.727
Senator Vreenak.

00:39:05.772 --> 00:39:07.364
He was returning to Romulus

00:39:07.407 --> 00:39:09.534
from a diplomatic mission
to Soukara

00:39:09.575 --> 00:39:10.667
when his shuttle exploded.

00:39:10.710 --> 00:39:13.338
The Tal Shiar are investigating

00:39:13.379 --> 00:39:15.347
but preliminary reports
point to sabotage.

00:39:15.381 --> 00:39:18.475
They believe that the Dominion
is responsible.

00:39:18.518 --> 00:39:22.545
The Dominion assassinated
a Romulan Senator.

00:39:22.588 --> 00:39:24.419
On a diplomatic mission.

00:39:24.457 --> 00:39:26.152
That changes everything.

00:39:26.192 --> 00:39:29.423
It could even bring the Romulans
into the war.

00:39:30.630 --> 00:39:32.655
Excuse me.

00:39:52.385 --> 00:39:53.579
Get up!

00:39:55.087 --> 00:39:56.179
You killed him!

00:39:56.222 --> 00:39:56.950
That's right.

00:39:56.989 --> 00:39:57.956
That's what you

00:39:57.990 --> 00:39:59.287
planned to do all along,
isn't it?

00:39:59.325 --> 00:40:01.316
You knew the data rod
wouldn't hold up to scrutiny.

00:40:01.360 --> 00:40:03.453
You just wanted
to get him on the station

00:40:03.496 --> 00:40:05.123
so that you could plant a bomb
on his shuttle!

00:40:05.164 --> 00:40:06.688
It wasn't quite that simple.

00:40:06.732 --> 00:40:09.963
I did have hopes that the rod
would somehow pass inspection

00:40:10.002 --> 00:40:11.435
but I suspected that Tolar

00:40:11.471 --> 00:40:13.234
may not have been
up to the task.

00:40:13.272 --> 00:40:15.433
And what about Tolar?
Did you kill him, too?!

00:40:15.475 --> 00:40:19.070
Think of them both
as tragic victims of war.

00:40:21.013 --> 00:40:23.777
If you can allow your anger
to subside for a moment

00:40:23.816 --> 00:40:26.512
you'll see
that they did not die in vain!

00:40:26.552 --> 00:40:28.713
The Romulans will enter the war!

00:40:28.754 --> 00:40:30.449
There's no guarantee of that!

00:40:30.490 --> 00:40:32.321
Oh, but I think that there is.

00:40:32.358 --> 00:40:34.792
You see, when the Tal Shiar
finishes examining

00:40:34.827 --> 00:40:36.385
the wreckage
of Vreenak's shuttle

00:40:36.429 --> 00:40:38.124
they'll find
the burnt remnants

00:40:38.164 --> 00:40:40.132
of a Cardassian
optolythic data rod

00:40:40.166 --> 00:40:43.135
which somehow miraculously
survived the explosion.

00:40:43.169 --> 00:40:45.763
After painstaking
forensic examination

00:40:45.805 --> 00:40:48.672
they'll discover that the rod
contains a recording

00:40:48.708 --> 00:40:50.676
of a high-level Dominion meeting

00:40:50.710 --> 00:40:53.838
at which the invasion of Romulus
was being planned.

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:56.508
And then they'll discover
that it is a fraud!

00:40:56.549 --> 00:40:58.312
Oh, I don't think they will

00:40:58.351 --> 00:41:00.945
because any imperfections
in the forgery

00:41:00.987 --> 00:41:04.286
will appear to be a result
of the explosion.

00:41:04.323 --> 00:41:08.123
So, with a seemingly legitimate
rod in one hand

00:41:08.160 --> 00:41:11.186
and a dead Senator
in the other...

00:41:11.230 --> 00:41:13.164
I ask you, Captain

00:41:13.199 --> 00:41:15.190
what conclusion would you draw?

00:41:16.736 --> 00:41:21.264
That Vreenak obtained the rod
on Soukara

00:41:21.307 --> 00:41:24.105
and that the Dominion killed him

00:41:24.143 --> 00:41:26.941
to prevent him from returning
to Romulus with it.

00:41:26.979 --> 00:41:28.503
Precisely.

00:41:28.548 --> 00:41:31.142
And the more the Dominion
protests its innocence

00:41:31.183 --> 00:41:33.743
the more the Romulans
will believe they're guilty

00:41:33.786 --> 00:41:35.777
because it's exactly
what the Romulans

00:41:35.821 --> 00:41:37.948
would have done in their place.

00:41:39.959 --> 00:41:42.484
That's why you came to me...

00:41:42.528 --> 00:41:44.496
isn't it, Captain?

00:41:44.530 --> 00:41:46.657
Because you knew

00:41:46.699 --> 00:41:48.599
I could do those things

00:41:48.634 --> 00:41:51.228
that you weren't capable
of doing.

00:41:51.270 --> 00:41:53.761
Well, it worked,
and you'll get what you want...

00:41:53.806 --> 00:41:56.104
a war between the Romulans
and the Dominion

00:41:56.142 --> 00:41:58.235
and if your conscience
is bothering you

00:41:58.277 --> 00:42:00.802
you should soothe it
with the knowledge

00:42:00.846 --> 00:42:02.677
that you may have just saved

00:42:02.715 --> 00:42:06.082
the entire Alpha Quadrant,
and all it cost

00:42:06.118 --> 00:42:08.746
was the life
of one Romulan Senator

00:42:08.788 --> 00:42:11.120
one criminal...

00:42:11.157 --> 00:42:17.323
and the self-respect
of one Starfleet Officer.

00:42:17.363 --> 00:42:20.059
I don't know about you

00:42:20.099 --> 00:42:23.933
but I'd call that a bargain.

00:42:23.970 --> 00:42:28.737
At 0800 hours, station time...

00:42:28.774 --> 00:42:31.607
the Romulan Empire
formally declared war

00:42:31.644 --> 00:42:33.669
against the Dominion.

00:42:33.713 --> 00:42:36.273
They have already struck
15 bases

00:42:36.315 --> 00:42:39.580
along the Cardassian border.

00:42:39.619 --> 00:42:40.984
So...

00:42:41.087 --> 00:42:44.523
this is a huge victory
for the good guys.

00:42:44.557 --> 00:42:49.494
This may even be the turning
point of the entire war.

00:42:49.528 --> 00:42:52.395
There is even
a "welcome to the fight" party

00:42:52.431 --> 00:42:53.989
tonight in the Wardroom.

00:42:54.066 --> 00:42:55.795
So...

00:42:58.270 --> 00:43:00.795
I lied.

00:43:00.840 --> 00:43:02.239
I cheated.

00:43:04.443 --> 00:43:09.312
I bribed men to cover the crimes
of other men.

00:43:12.485 --> 00:43:15.420
I am an accessory to murder.

00:43:17.189 --> 00:43:19.817
But the most damning thing
of all...

00:43:21.594 --> 00:43:23.824
I think I can live with it.

00:43:25.765 --> 00:43:28.233
And if I had to do it
all over again...

00:43:29.702 --> 00:43:31.033
I would.

00:43:32.872 --> 00:43:36.069
Garak was right about one thing.

00:43:36.108 --> 00:43:39.635
A guilty conscience
is a small price

00:43:39.679 --> 00:43:43.740
to pay for the safety
of the Alpha Quadrant

00:43:43.783 --> 00:43:46.650
so I will learn...

00:43:46.686 --> 00:43:48.415
to live with it.

00:43:55.561 --> 00:43:57.893
Because I can live with it.

00:44:01.834 --> 00:44:04.029
I can live with it.

00:44:12.878 --> 00:44:13.970
Computer...

00:44:15.981 --> 00:44:18.983
erase that entire personal log.
